@page "/denied"
@*
    Shown when a signed-in user reaches a page their role does not cover.

    Routable as well as embeddable, because the two ways of being refused arrive differently: Blazor pages
    render this through Routes.razor's NotAuthorized slot, while the /admin/* minimal-API endpoints are
    refused by the cookie handler, which can only redirect — so it needs a URL to redirect to.

    Before roles existed, NotAuthorized could only mean "not signed in", so Routes.razor sent every case
    to RedirectToLogin. That is wrong for a Viewer who is already authenticated: they would be bounced to
    a login page they have no way to satisfy — the credentials they hold are not the problem — and login
    would send them straight back. Distinguishing the two cases is what makes a role denial legible.
*@
<div class="page-header">
    <h1>Not available to your account</h1>
</div>

<p class="muted">
    You're signed in as <strong>@_name</strong>@(_role is null ? "" : $" ({_role})"), and this page needs a
    higher level of access. If you need it, ask an administrator of this instance to change your role.
</p>

<div class="actions">
    <a href="/" class="btn">Back to the dashboard</a>
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private Task<AuthenticationState>? AuthState { get; set; }

    private string _name = "this account";
    private string? _role;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        if (AuthState is null) return;

        var user = (await AuthState).User;
        if (user.Identity?.Name is { Length: > 0 } n) _name = n;
        _role = user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.Role)?.Value;
    }
}
